    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n10469" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Consentĭa</span></b> ,
		ae, f., = <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">Κωνσεντία</span>, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>the capital of the Bruttii</i>, now <i>Cōsenza</i>, <i><span class="en">Mel. 2, 4,
			8</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. 3, 5, 10, § 72</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Liv. 8,
				24, 14 sq.</span></i>; <i><span class="en">23, 30, 5 al.</span></i>—Hence, <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Consentīnus</span></b> , a, um,
				<i>adj., of</i> or <i>pertaining to
				Consentia</i>: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ager,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Varr. R. R. 1, 7, 6</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">Plin. 16, 27, 50, §
			115</span></i>.—And <b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">Consentini</span></b> , ōrum, m.,
				<i>the inhabitants of Consentia</i>, Cic Fin. 1,
			3, 7.</div>
